<h2>Original 2021 nine-card number-line classification</h2>
<p>This is an independent mathematical reconstruction, <strong>not the publisher's graphics</strong>. Divide the ENTIRE span by the number of equal intervals; printed endpoints matter. Students may choose different mathematically defensible groups.</p>
<table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Original card</th><th scope="col">Endpoints</th><th scope="col">Equal spaces</th><th scope="col">Space length</th><th scope="col">Independent tick values</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">A</th><td>0 to 8</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>0, 4, 8</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">B</th><td>0 to 1</td><td>4</td><td>1/4</td><td>0, 1/4, 2/4, 3/4, 1</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">C</th><td>0 to 3</td><td>6</td><td>1/2</td><td>0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2, 5/2, 3</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">D</th><td>0 to 2</td><td>4</td><td>1/2</td><td>0, 1/2, 1, 3/2, 2</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">E</th><td>0 to 4</td><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>0, 1, 2, 3, 4</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">F</th><td>0 to 1</td><td>6</td><td>1/6</td><td>0, 1/6, 2/6, 3/6, 4/6, 5/6, 1</td></tr>
